Ben's Food Court: Game Design Proposal
A proposal for the bigger game built around Ben's Burger Bar. Everything here is a starting point for Ari, Bryan and Tabby to decide on. The hub rulebook, ACCESSIBILITY.md, still outranks everything.
The big picture
Ben's Food Court is a mall food court seen from above. Each storefront is its own restaurant game, built like the Burger Bar. The player picks a restaurant, works shifts there, and earns stars. The goal is to get every restaurant to five stars and packed with customers.
The restaurants:
1. Ben's Burger Bar
2. Ben's Pizza Parlor
3. Ben's Smoothie Shack
4. Ben's Cafe (coffee and donuts)
5. Ben's Sushi
6. Ben's Burritos
7. Ben's Ice Cream Emporium
All seven are in. The Burger Bar, Pizza Parlor and Cafe are open from the start, and the other four open one at a time as ratings improve (see Unlocking restaurants).
The food court screen
A top-down cartoon view of the court, in the same cel-shaded style as the games. Each storefront shows its status at a glance, using real objects rather than floating UI, as in the Burger Bar.
• Stars: a star sign above each storefront (one to five stars).
• Popularity: shown by the crowd. A quiet restaurant has one or two people wandering past; a popular one has a line out the door and full tables. This reads at a glance and doesn't need numbers.
• Status: a restaurant that isn't open yet has its shutter down with a "Coming Soon" sign, a newly opened one gets a "Grand Opening" banner, and one at five stars gets a gold sign.
• The goal: when all seven restaurants reach five stars, the whole court throws a big celebration.
There is one main menu for the whole food court, and it replaces the Burger Bar's current main menu. Selecting a restaurant zooms into it and goes straight to the counter view, with no separate menu for each restaurant.
Scanning the court
